entry.summary:
Prisma is the best ORM for Next.js projects. Type-safe queries, auto-generated types, clean migrations — it makes working with databases feel like working with TypeScript objects. Here's the complete setup. npm install prisma @prisma/client npx prisma init
This creates: prisma/schema.prisma — your database schema .env — with DATABASE_URL placeholder // prisma/schema.prisma generator client { provider = "prisma-client-js" }
datasource db { provider = "postgresql" url = env("DATABASE_URL") }
model User { id String @id @default(cuid()) name String email String @unique password String role Role @default(USER) createdAt DateTime @default(now()) updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt
posts Post[] profile Profile?
@@index([email]) }
…
